model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Account checks and usage attempts retain only a closed failure source, reason, validated optional provider HTTP status and failure time. Failed refreshes preserve the last successful reading; a first failure needs no reading. Management and transport failures never claim a provider status. Public health, usage, details and logs exclude raw responses, headers, credentials, backend references and vendor request IDs. Health checks preserve identity and failure detail across restart; recovery clears failed-check metadata while preserving that identity. Successful refreshes clear the prior attempt failure; old records retain their generic explanation. Diagnostic failure matrices run separately from acquisition lifecycle proof so repeated restart and UI work stays within each unchanged scenario deadline. The carried source follows the pinned formatter while preserving its typed behavior and test assertions."
    }
  }
}
